quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  6,9,"And if We had sent an angel himself (as a messenger), We would have surely sent him as a man, and (even in that case) We would have put them in the same doubt which they already are in (i.e. being confused over his physical appearance, they would say: ‘He is just a man like us.’)"
  6,10,"(Other) messengers had already been mocked before you (Esteemed Prophet). Then, those who mocked them were besieged by what they used to ridicule."
  6,11,"Say: ‘Travel through the land, then see how the end of the deniers was.’"
  6,12,"Say: ‘To whom belongs all that is in the heavens and the earth?’ Say: ‘To Allah.’ He has prescribed mercy upon Himself (as a gracious obligation). He will surely gather you on the Day of Resurrection, in which there is no doubt. Those who have ruined themselves will never believe."
  6,13,"And to Him belongs whatever rests in the night and the day. And He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing."
  6,14,"Say: ‘Shall I take (someone) as guardian other than Allah, the Originator of the heavens and the earth, Who feeds and is not fed,’ Say: ‘I have been commanded to be the first who submits himself (to Allah). And you should not be among the polytheists.’"
  6,15,"Say: ‘Indeed, I fear—if I were to disobey my Lord—the punishment of a tremendous Day.’"
  6,16,"Whoever is spared (from the punishment) on that Day, He has surely shown His Mercy to him, and that is the manifest success."
  6,17,"And if Allah afflicts you with some suffering, no one can remove it except Him, and if He bestows some good upon you, then He is All-Capable of everything."
  6,18,"And He is Dominant over His servants, and He is the All-Wise, the All-Aware."
